    {
      "beat_id": "B00",
      "act": "ASK",
      "narration_text": "A robot sat a test with ten questions, and got every single one wrong. Zero out of ten. But here is the strange part — the robot was never switched on. This is Humanitarians AI. Today we find out who actually failed that test.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "Who failed the test?",
            "topic": "A STORY ABOUT MARKING",
            "segment": "The Test Where Everybody Got Zero",
            "command": "A robot answered ten questions and scored zero on all of them. Before I blame the robot, check the test itself — the marking rules, the tidying step, and whether the robot was ever actually asked anything.",
            "runningText": "checking the test…",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "the marking rule is stricter than it looks",
              "the tidying machine eats letters",
              "and the robot was fast asleep"
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B00.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.9,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B00.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.51,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B00.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "MEET",
      "narration_text": "First, meet the robot. You ask it a question, and it gives you an answer. What is the capital of France? Paris. What is three plus four? Seven. So far, easy.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidRobotTest",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.9,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.18,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidRobotTest",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "MARKER",
      "narration_text": "But somebody has to decide whether each answer counts as right. That is the marker's job. And this marker follows one very strict rule.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "THE MARKER",
            "headline": "Every test needs someone to say right or wrong.",
            "kicker": "and this one has a rule it never bends"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.2,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.51,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "RULE",
      "narration_text": "The rule is this: your answer has to match the correct word exactly. Say Paris, and you get a tick. Say, the capital of France is Paris, and you get a cross. Same city. Different mark.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidStampRule",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13.8,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.56,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidStampRule",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "GUM",
      "narration_text": "And here is why. When the marker compares two answers, it chops them into words. But the full stop stays stuck to the last word, like chewing gum. So paris-with-a-dot and paris look like two completely different words. The answer was perfect. The score was zero.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidGumDot",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 17.7,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.7,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidGumDot",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "NAMING",
      "narration_text": "Grown-ups call that strict rule exact match. It only says yes when every single letter lines up.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "WHAT IT IS CALLED",
            "headline": "Exact match: every letter, or nothing.",
            "kicker": "one small dot is enough to fail"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 6.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 6.02,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "PARTIAL",
      "narration_text": "There is a kinder way to mark. Instead of all or nothing, count how many words match. Answer Delhi when the right answer is New Delhi, and you got one word out of two. That earns about two thirds of a mark, instead of nothing at all.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "EvalTokenOverlap",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 18.1,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.7,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:EvalTokenOverlap",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "MONSTER",
      "narration_text": "Now the strangest problem of the lot. Before anything is marked, every answer goes through a cleaning machine. It is meant to tidy the words up. But it only keeps the letters a to z. Feed it Brasília, the capital of Brazil, and it eats the letter with the accent. What comes out is bras, space, lia.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidLetterMonster",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B07.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 21.9,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 18.47,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidLetterMonster",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "CONSEQUENCE",
      "narration_text": "The machine snapped the city in half. And it does this to the correct answer too. So no spelling of Brasília can ever match — not the fancy one, not the plain one, not even the right one.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "NOBODY CAN WIN",
            "headline": "It breaks the answer key as well.",
            "kicker": "a question that is impossible to get right"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B08.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14.6,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.14,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "SLEEPY",
      "narration_text": "And then the big one. Look at what the robot actually said. Every answer, all ten of them, was the same two words: mock output. The robot was never switched on.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidSleepyRobot",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B09.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.9,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.11,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidSleepyRobot",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "act": "WHY",
      "narration_text": "The test needed a special key to wake the robot up, and there was no key. So instead of stopping and saying so, the programme quietly pretended, and carried on as if nothing was wrong.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "WHY IT HAPPENED",
            "headline": "It did not crash. It pretended.",
            "kicker": "a silent failure is worse than a loud one"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B10.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.48,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "act": "PARADE",
      "narration_text": "Ten questions. Ten identical answers. Ten zeros. And at the end, the computer drew a tidy chart of the results — four bars, all flat at nothing.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidZeroParade",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 10.4,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.79,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidZeroParade",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "act": "DANGER",
      "narration_text": "That chart is the dangerous bit. It has a title. It has labels. It has neat straight edges. It looks exactly like a finished piece of work. It simply does not mean anything at all.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "THE DANGEROUS PART",
            "headline": "It looks finished. That is the problem.",
            "kicker": "a chart of nothing still looks like a chart"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B12.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.5,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B12.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B13",
      "act": "LESSON",
      "narration_text": "So here is the big idea, and it is worth keeping. When every single answer comes back wrong, do not start by blaming whoever was answering. Check the test.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "THE BIG IDEA",
            "headline": "When everyone fails, check the test.",
            "kicker": "zero out of ten is a clue, not a result"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B13.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.2,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B13.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.01,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B13.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B14",
      "act": "CHECK",
      "narration_text": "You can check a marker the same way you check anything else. Hand it an answer you already know is right, and watch what it says. Paris, when the answer is Paris — fine. Paris with a full stop — wrong. Brasilia — wrong. Two out of three. The marker is broken.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidTestTheTeacher",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B14.mp4",
            "at": "2026-09-25T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 20.0,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B14.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.51,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B14.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidTestTheTeacher",
        "at": "2026-09-25T11:47:53"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B15",
      "act": "CHEAP",
      "narration_text": "That takes about a minute. One minute, and you would have caught every single problem in this story before anybody ever looked at a chart.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "IT IS CHEAP",
